    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T19:29:47Z",
    "body": "Cause found (M5). On a host where two OS users build with sccache, both users use the default sccache port 4226. One user starts the sccache server first and owns the port. The builds of the other user then connect to a server that is not theirs, and fail with \"Failed to read response header\" or \"Failed to send data to or receive data from server\". This occurred on uma: the runner user `ghrunner` and the `mikekinney` build pools (started 2026-11-14) shared the port. A restart of the other user's server also stops the runner build.\n\nFix applied on the mkinney machines (not in the repository):\n- The runner `.env` on uma, len and m3 now sets `SCCACHE_SERVER_PORT=4227` and `SCCACHE_IDLE_TIMEOUT=0`. The runner has its own sccache server, and the server does not stop when idle.\n- The runners on uma and m3 were restarted. The runner on len is stopped at this time.\n\nFor the cut runner and other self-hosted runners: give the runner user its own `SCCACHE_SERVER_PORT` in its `.env` if another user on the same host also builds with sccache. The \"Done means\" item of this issue (the gate falls back to plain rustc when sccache answers an error) is still open.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
